## Why This Is Asked
This question tests proficiency with partition dynamic programming where subarrays must be non-overlapping and values derive from range statistics. The solution requires careful separation of concerns: precomputing range queries, implementing the DP transition, and reconstructing the solution through pointer tracking.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping contiguous subarrays as partition elements
- Dynamic programming with two-dimensional state tracking
- Range minima preprocessing for O(1) query access
- Solution reconstruction through backpointers
- Complexity optimization through careful algorithm design

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraysMin(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;

  // Precompute range minima
  const mins = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let m = Infinity;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[j]);
      mins[i][j] = m;
    }
  }
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests DP over partitions with a non-linear block cost dependent on average, plus reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP over k blocks
- Prefix sums for O(1) block sums
- Non-linear, floor(sum/len) cost
- Backtracking for endpoints
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartition(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const INF = 1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(INF));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const sum = pref[i]-pref[p];
        const len = i-p;
        const cost = Math.floor(sum/len);
        if(dp[p][t-1] + cost < dp[i][t]){
          dp[i][t] = dp[p][t-1] + cost;
          par[i][t] = p;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  let blocks = [], i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const p = par[i][t];
    blocks.push([p+1, i]);
    i = p; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize to faster than O(n^2 k)?
- How to handle negatives or alternative cost such as max/min?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests minimax-style DP with reconstruction for a classic game.

## Key Concepts
- Two-player DP with difference state
- Subarray DP and reconstruction path
- Time: O(n^2) space: O(n^2)

## Code Example
```javascript
// dp[i][j] denotes max diff for i..j
function maxFirstPlayer(values){
  const n = values.length; const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  let total = values.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][i]=values[i];
  for(let len=2; len<=n; len++){
    for(let i=0;i+len-1<n;i++){
      const j=i+len-1;
      dp[i][j] = Math.max(values[i]-dp[i+1][j], values[j]-dp[i][j-1]);
    }
  }
  return (total + dp[0][n-1])/2;
}
```

