## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over time with multiple constraints: multiple transactions, reconstruction, and edge-case handling.

## Key Concepts
- Two DP states: cash (not holding) and hold (holding).
- Transitions model buy/sell with transaction count t.
- Base cases initialize day 0; backtracking recovers trade days.
- Space optimization possible to O(k) with rolling arrays.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxProfit(prices, k){
  const n = prices.length;
  if (n===0 || k===0) return 0;
  const cash = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const hold = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) cash[0][t] = (t===0)?0:-1e15;
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++){
    for (let t=0; t<=k; t++){
      cash[i][t] = cash[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) cash[i][t] = Math.max(cash[i][t], hold[i-1][t] + prices[i-1]);
      hold[i][t] = hold[i-1][t];
      if (t>0) hold[i][t] = Math.max(hold[i][t], cash[i-1][t-1] - prices[i-1]);
    }
  }
  let best = 0;
  for (let t=0; t<=k; t++) best = Math.max(best, cash[n][t]);
  return best;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you recover the exact trade days from the DP table?
- How does the solution change if k >= n/2 (unlimited transactions)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with adjacency constraint and exact count; requires states over i and j, base cases, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- DP with two dimensions n and k
- adjacency constraint via i-2 transition
- reconstruction via parent pointers or decisions
- space/time bounds and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumNoAdj(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const K = Math.min(k, Math.floor((n + 1) / 2));
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(K + 1).fill(0));
  const take = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(K + 1).fill(false));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j <= K; j++) {
      dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j];
      if (j > 0) {
        if (i >= 2) {
          const cand = dp[i - 2][j - 1] + A[i - 1];
          if (cand > dp[i][j]) {
            dp[i][j] = cand;
            take[i][j] = true;
          }
        } else if (i === 1 && j === 1) {
          if (A[0] > dp[i][j]) { dp[i][j] = A[0]; take[i][j] = true; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let i = n, j = K, indices = [];
  while (i >= 1 && j >= 0) {
    if (take[i][j]) { indices.push(i - 1); i -= 2; j -= 1; }
    else { i -= 1; }
  }
  indices.reverse();
  return { sum: dp[n][K], indices };
}
```

